#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid "Designing Forms"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "Most important terms"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: designingforms.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "Form"
msgstr "Formulari"

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "A window provided for easy data entry and presentation on the computer screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: designingforms.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "Form's data source"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Database table or query providing data displayed in the form. The data source "
"is needed because forms itself are only <emphasis>tools</emphasis> "
"for displaying and entering data, while tables and queries are the source of "
"data. New, empty forms have no data source assigned, so they are not displaying "
"any data from your database unless you assign a data source to them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: designingforms.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Form field"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Direct equivalent of a column in a table or query. Most frequently used are "
"fields for displaying text and numbers. Entering a new value or changing the "
"existing value of such a field causes a change in the bound table or query "
"column (after accepting the change)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: designingforms.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "Form design"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tasks you are performing to define the appearance and functions of the form. To "
"do this, you need to provide <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-data-source\">"
"data source</glossterm>, insert <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">"
"form fields</glossterm> of various types and place them at the appropriate "
"location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: designingforms.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "Form widget"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "Form's element. Main widget types are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Widgets displaying information, &eg; a text box or an image box. Each widget of "
"this type can be <emphasis>bound</emphasis> to a data source field (a table or "
"a query column). Therefore, such widgets are called in short <glossterm "
"linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">form fields</glossterm>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Widgets able to perform a specified action, &eg; a push button that can close "
"the current form. Within other applications this widget type is sometimes "
"called <firstterm>form control</firstterm> because it can perform previously "
"defined action of <emphasis>controlling</emphasis> your database application's "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Other widgets allowing to enrich a form's appearance, &eg; a <quote>"
"line widget</quote> can visually separate two form areas."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: designingforms.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "Container widget"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A widget that can <emphasis>contain</emphasis> other widgets within its area. "
"For example, frame widget or tab widget are containers. The form's surface "
"itself is a container as well. A command button cannot be called as container "
"because it is not possible to insert a widget inside it. In more complex cases, "
"container widgets can be inserted inside a container, so nesting is possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "Forms versus tables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In chapter 5.2 you learned about how to enter data directly into tables using "
"their data sheet view. However, in many cases forms are better suited for data "
"entry:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A table can contain too many columns to display them on your screen. A form can "
"display such a data using multiple rows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A form allows to visually split data <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">"
"fields</glossterm> into logical groups, thus increasing readability. Labels "
"with additional information can be inserted to give users more hints on how to "
"use the form or what given data <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">"
"fields</glossterm> mean."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Command buttons can be used within forms for commonly used commands so users "
"can use forms in a similar way as a standalone applications they know."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In data sheet view displaying multi-row data text <glossterm "
"linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">fields</glossterm> or images is as easy as within "
"forms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working with form design"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As with table or query design, you are able to use <interface>"
"Data View</interface> and <interface>Design View</interface>"
". Form designing is performed in <interface>Design View</interface>"
". We will often refer to the form design window as to <interface>"
"Form Designer</interface>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new empty form, select <menuchoice><guimenu>Insert</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem> Form</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the Menubar. Optionally, you "
"can use <menuchoice><guimenuitem> New Form</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"command from drop-down button on the <interface>Project Navigator's</interface> "
"toolbar or <menuchoice><guimenuitem>Create Object: Form</guimenuitem>"
"</menuchoice> command from the context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A new frame will appear, you can resize the form by moving the borders. The "
"form is covered with a grid which simplifies accurate positioning of the "
"widgets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As with table design, <interface>Form Designer</interface> provides <interface>"
"Property pane</interface>. To save some space on the screen, the pane has three "
"tabs related to the currently selected form:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: designingforms.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Properties</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Contains a list of properties for the currently selected widget."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: designingforms.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Data source</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Contains properties related specifically to the <glossterm "
"linkend=\"gloss-form-data-source\">data source</glossterm> "
"of the currently selected widget or the form itself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: designingforms.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Widgets</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Contains a hierarchy of all widgets of the form. The list simplifies widgets "
"lookup by name and navigation between them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is information about currently selected widget's name and type displayed "
"on the first and second tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Additional toolbars are also available:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Widgets</guilabel> toolbar used for inserting new widgets into "
"the form"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Format</guilabel> toolbar used to format form's elements (&eg; "
"adjusting widget's size, grouping). Formatting commands are also available in "
"the <guimenu>Format</guimenu> menu. More about these commands can be found in "
"<xref linkend=\"formatmenu\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the <guilabel>Widgets</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Widgets</guilabel> tab in the <interface>Property pane</interface> "
"provides a list of form widgets and their hierarchy. Each widget is presented "
"within the hierarchy beside other widgets being on the same level (the same "
"parent container). Child widgets (inside containers) are presented using "
"indented names."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each widget has displayed its name and type. The type has also an icon "
"displayed - the same as the one displayed on the toolbar used while form "
"designing is performed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changing the current selection on the list causes appropriate selection on the "
"designed form. This allows for easier widget lookup by name and easier "
"navigation. For example, it is possible to select a widget by name, and then "
"switch to the <guilabel>Properties</guilabel> tab to change the widget's "
"properties."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keeping the <keycap>Ctrl</keycap> key pressed while an item on the widgets list "
"is being selected allows to select multiple widgets at a time. Keeping the "
"<keycap>Shift</keycap> key pressed allows to select entire lists of widgets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Giving widgets reasonable names can be useful but is not mandatory. Note that "
"widget's name is a property that is not visible to the user of your form. Users "
"will only see a widget text, provided by <varname>Text</varname> "
"property or similar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inserting widgets - text fields"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's create a form providing information about persons, i.e. a form connected "
"it with <literal>Persons</literal> table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the form being designed should present data obtained from the database, you "
"need to place appropriate <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">"
"fields</glossterm> on it. To do this, use the buttons on the <guilabel>"
"Widgets</guilabel> toolbar. Each button corresponds to a single widget type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Text Box</guibutton> button on the <guilabel>Widgets</guilabel> "
"toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the form surface with the <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> "
"mouse button. A new text box widget will be placed in the point where you "
"clicked. Before you release you can drag your mouse to specify a desired size "
"for the widget."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If needed, move the inserted widget using drag &amp; drop to a desired "
"position. You can resize the widget afterwards by dragging one of the small "
"boxes appearing near its corners. Note that the boxes are only visible when the "
"widget is selected. If you select another widget or the form surface, the boxes "
"disappear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>Text Box</guibutton> toolbar button again and click on the "
"form surface to insert another widget. Repeat this action once again until you "
"get three text boxes inserted in your form. For sake of simplicity we will "
"limit ourselves to three data <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">"
"fields</glossterm>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a context menu available in form's design mode, activated by a "
"<mousebutton>right</mousebutton> mouse button click the desired widget or the "
"form's surface. The menu offers commands like <guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem>"
", <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem>"
", <guimenuitem>Delete</guimenuitem> and other, more complex. Many of the "
"commands are also provided in the <guilabel>Menubar</guilabel>"
", usually <guimenuitem>Edit</guimenuitem>. Keyboard shortcuts are also "
"available for these commands. Some of the commands are only available for "
"certain types of widgets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The commands <guimenuitem> Cut</guimenuitem>,<guimenuitem> Copy</guimenuitem> "
"and <guimenuitem> Paste</guimenuitem> makes it possible to move or copy widgets "
"between forms, even between separate database projects."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Holding the <keycap>Ctrl</keycap> key down while clicking a widget allows to "
"select multiple widgets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Instead of using <guimenuitem> Copy</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem> "
"Paste</guimenuitem> commands, to duplicate a widget within the same form you "
"can hold down the <keycap>Ctrl</keycap> key while moving the widget. After the "
"<keycap>Ctrl</keycap> key is released, the dragged widget will not be moved but "
"copied in the new location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid "Assigning data sources"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">fields</glossterm> "
"you inserted have no <emphasis>data source</emphasis> "
"assigned yet, so these are not able to display information from the database. "
"To assign data source, use the <guilabel>Data Source</guilabel> "
"tab of the <interface>Property pane</interface>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The very first step is to specify the <glossterm "
"linkend=\"gloss-form-data-source\">form's data source</glossterm>"
", i.e. a place the displayed data will be fetched from. As mentioned above, you "
"will use table <literal>persons</literal> as a <glossterm "
"linkend=\"gloss-form-data-source\">data source</glossterm> for your new form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the form's surface, as you will alter its properties."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Switch to the <guilabel>Data Source</guilabel> tab and enter <literal>"
"persons</literal> table name in the <guilabel>Form's data source</guilabel> "
"drop down list. Alternatively, you can select this name from the drop down "
"list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You have assigned <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-data-source\">"
"form's data source</glossterm>. Now you need to do specify widget's data "
"source."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the first text field widget at the top of the form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Data Source</guilabel> tab of the property pane enter field "
"name <varname>name</varname> in the <emphasis>Widget's data source</emphasis> "
"drop down list. Alternatively, you can select this name from the drop down "
"list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on next text field widget and enter <varname>surname</varname> "
"as the data source."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter data sources for <varname>street</varname>, <varname>"
"house_number</varname> and <varname>city</varname> text <glossterm "
"linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">fields</glossterm> in a similar way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can now save the form's design (this is not mandatory to test the form in "
"action). To save, click the <guilabel>Save object changes</guilabel> "
"toolbar button or use the <menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">"
"<keycap>Ctrl</keycap><keycap>S</keycap></keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>"
"File</guimenu><guimenuitem> Save</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"menu command. Upon saving you will be asked for entering the form's name. Enter "
"<literal>Persons</literal> as caption and click the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> "
"button. The form's name will be filled automatically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:514
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the right moment for testing your form. Click the <guibutton>"
"Switch to data view</guibutton> toolbar button. Unless you made a mistake while "
"entering data sources, you should see <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-field\">"
"form's fields</glossterm> filled with data from the <literal>persons</literal> "
"table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to remove widget's <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-data-source\">"
"data source</glossterm> assignment for a form widget, you can use <guibutton>"
"Clear widget's data source</guibutton> button near the <guilabel>"
"Widet's data source</guilabel> drop down list. Similarly, you can use the "
"<guibutton>Clear form's data source</guibutton> button near the <guilabel>"
"Form's data source</guilabel> drop down list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the <guibutton>Go to selected form's data source</guibutton> "
"button to select appropriate table or query in the <interface>"
"Project Navigator</interface>, so you can quickly open a table or query being "
"the <glossterm linkend=\"gloss-form-data-source\">data source</glossterm> "
"of the form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:561
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inserting text labels"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To make it easier for the form's user to identify the meaning of every field "
"widget, these should have added text labels with appropriate titles. To create "
"text labels the <literal>Label</literal> widget is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:568
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Insert three text label widgets onto the form, placing them on the left side of "
"the text fields (or on the right hand if your operating system uses "
"right-to-left layout). On inserting a new label, a text cursor appears at the "
"location where you can enter the desired title. Enter consecutively: <literal>"
"Name</literal>, <literal>Surname</literal> and <literal>Street</literal>"
". Additionally, on the top of the form insert another label displaying name of "
"the form, i.e. <literal>Persons</literal>. Enlarge this label's size and and "
"increase the font size using <menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Font...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:595
#, no-c-format
msgid "Actions"
msgstr "Accions"

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An <literal>Action</literal> is a single activity isolated in the application, "
"available for the user to execute. It can also be executed automatically as a "
"reaction for a given event (&eg; after opening a form)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid "Assigning actions to form buttons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many actions can be assigned to form button. The assigned action is executed "
"after button is clicked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid "To assign action:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid "Switch to form's <interface>Design view</interface> if you have not done yet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the existing button widget by clicking on it or put a new button widget "
"onto the form. If you inserted a new button, enter its title and press "
"<keycombo action=\"press\"><keycap>Enter</keycap></keycombo> key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the button widget with the <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> "
"mouse button to display the context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From the context menu select <guimenuitem>Assign action...</guimenuitem> "
"command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An <guilabel>Assigning Action to Command Button</guilabel> "
"dialog window will appear presenting a list of available actions. One of the "
"actions is selected if the widget already has action assigned. Otherwise the "
"<guilabel>Action type</guilabel> drop down list has the <guilabel>"
"No type</guilabel> item selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From the <guilabel>Action type</guilabel> drop down list select <guilabel>"
"Application</guilabel> item. Available application-wide actions will be listed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select one of the actions on the list (&eg; <guilabel>Delete Row</guilabel>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:653
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button or press the <keycombo "
"action=\"press\"><keycap>Enter</keycap></keycombo> key to accept your "
"selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:671
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After switching to the form's <emphasis>data view</emphasis> "
"you can try whether the action works. For example, if you assigned <guilabel>"
"Delete Row</guilabel> action, clicking the button, the current database row "
"will be deleted, similarly to executing <menuchoice><shortcut>"
"<keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>Ctrl</keycap><keycap>Delete</keycap>"
"</keycombo></shortcut><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Delete Row</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu command (depending on your settings "
"you may be asked to confirm the removal)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:682
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove an action assignment, select <guilabel>No type</guilabel> "
"item from the <guilabel>Action type</guilabel> drop down list of the <guilabel>"
"Assigning Action to Command Button</guilabel> dialog window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:689
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Actions only work in the form's <emphasis>data view</emphasis>"
". Not every action's assignment is reasonable. For example, the <guimenuitem>"
"Font...</guimenuitem> action is available in data view, but only if you have a "
"widget selected in the <interface>Design view</interface>"
". If you make changes to the font settings the changes are applied to the text "
"of that selected widget."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:704
#, no-c-format
msgid "Widget layouts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:705
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In most cases form widgets should be conveniently arranged and aligned. "
"Positioning, aligning and resizing widgets by hand is not easy and these "
"parameters are not adjusted when the user resizes the form. In fact the "
"situation is even worse because you cannot assume a given form requires a given "
"space because users have different font sizes and display resolutions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using special tool called widget layouts can help to automatically lay out the "
"form widgets. Widget layout is an action of grouping two or more widgets so "
"these are well positioned and have appropriate sizes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:733
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using layout in a form improves alignment. Moreover, its space is better used. "
"Text fields are closer to each other, spacing is constant."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:748
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two methods to create widget layout."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select two or more widgets that should be placed in a common layout, and select "
"one of the layout types from the context menu item <guilabel>"
"Layout Widgets</guilabel> ."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:760
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click a container widget (or a form surface itself), where widgets are inserted "
"and select one of the layout types from the context menu item Layout Widgets . "
"All widgets existing within the container or within the form, being on the same "
"level will be put into a single common layout."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:770
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In each of these cases you can also use <menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Layout Widgets</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:808
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Widget layout is presented in the design view using a blue, green or red box "
"drawn with a broken line. This line is displayed only in the form's design "
"view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:824
#, no-c-format
msgid "Besides the grid type, there are other widget layout types."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: designingforms.docbook:827
#, no-c-format
msgid "vertical"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:829
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vertical widget layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: designingforms.docbook:844
#, no-c-format
msgid "horizontal"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:846
#, no-c-format
msgid "Horizontal widget layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:869
#, no-c-format
msgid "Springs in widget layouts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:870
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <emphasis>spring</emphasis> in widget layouts is a special, invisible element "
"allowing to adjust widget's position and size within layouts. Such a spring "
"stretches or squeezes a widget on the right, top, bottom or left hand, so it "
"can have desired size and position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:876
#, no-c-format
msgid "To use a spring:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:879
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select spring icon on the <guilabel>Widgets</guilabel> toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:885
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on a selected point of the form to insert the spring."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:905
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To make springs work you need to create a global widget layout, i.e. a layout "
"for the form itself. Then, springs can use edges of the form as a boundary for "
"expanding."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:984
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removing widget layouts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:985
#, no-c-format
msgid "To remove widget layout without removing widgets, perform one of these actions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:991
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click with the <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> mouse button on the layout's "
"border and select <guimenuitem>Break Layout</guimenuitem> "
"command from the context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:998
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click with the <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> mouse button on the layout's "
"border and select <menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Break Layout</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1007
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Removing widget layout using the <guimenuitem>Break Layout</guimenuitem> "
"command will not remove widgets contained in the layout. If you want to remove "
"the widgets as well, just select the layout by clicking on its border and press "
"<keycap>Delete</keycap> key or use <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem> Delete</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu command or context menu "
"command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:1020
#, no-c-format
msgid "Size policies for widgets within a layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1021
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Instead of setting a fixed size for your widgets, in &kexi; you can choose "
"between various widget's size policies. A <emphasis>size policy</emphasis> "
"is a flexible strategy for controlling how a widget is stretched (or shrunk) "
"depending on other neighbouring widgets and space available within the form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1027
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After putting widgets into a <emphasis>layout</emphasis>"
", typically each widget gets a proportional (<guilabel>Preferred</guilabel>"
") size policy. These widgets will be automatically resized with preferred "
"settings, depending on their type and size of the entire layout itself. For "
"example, three buttons put into the horizontal layout will be resized to fit "
"their visible text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1034
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For each widget inserted into the form, there are settings for size policy "
"available in the <interface>Property Editor</interface>"
". The settings are presented as a group of properties called <guilabel>"
"Size Policy</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1049
#, no-c-format
msgid "This group of properties contains:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1052
#, no-c-format
msgid "Horizontal Size Policy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1054
#, no-c-format
msgid "defining horizontal size of the widget,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1058
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vertical Size Policy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1060
#, no-c-format
msgid "defining vertical size of the widget,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1064
#, no-c-format
msgid "Horizontal Stretch"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1066
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"defining strength of activity of the <guilabel>Horizontal Size Policy</guilabel>"
","
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1073
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vertical Stretch"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1075
#, no-c-format
msgid "defining strength of activity of the <guilabel>Vertical Size Policy</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:1084
#, no-c-format
msgid "Values of size policies"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1085
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following values are available in the drop down list for <guilabel>"
"Horizontal Size Policy</guilabel> and <guilabel>Vertical Size Policy</guilabel> "
"properties visible in the <interface>Property Editor</interface>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1093
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fixed"
msgstr "Fixe"

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1095
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"this value means that the widget cannot be automatically resized; it should "
"maintain the constant size defined at design time (width or height),"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimum"
msgstr "Minim"

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"this value means that the original size of the widget is set as minimal "
"allowed, it is sufficient and there is no need for expanding the widget, but "
"the widget will be expanded if needed. This type of policy can be used to force "
"the widget to be expanded to the whole width or height, especially if you set a "
"stretch value greater than 0."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Maximum"
msgstr "Maxim"

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"this value means that the original size of the widget is set as maximum allowed "
"and can be decreased without breaking the widget's usability and readability if "
"other widgets need more space,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1135
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preferred"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"this value means that the original size of the widget is the best and "
"preferred; the widget can be shrunk or expanded however and it will stay "
"readable,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1156
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expanding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"this value means that the original size of the widget is reasonable but the "
"widget can be also shrunk; it can be expanded as well to take as much space as "
"possible,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1166
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimum Expanding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"this value means that the original size of the widget is allowed; it can be "
"expanded to take as much space as possible,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ignored"
msgstr "Ignorat"

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"this value means that the original size of the widget is ignored; the widget "
"can be expanded to take as much space as possible but other widgets usually "
"will not allow for that"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Different widget types have various default size policies; for example, button "
"widgets have default size policy set to <guilabel>Minimum</guilabel> "
"(in both directions), while text field widgets have vertical size policy set to "
"<guilabel>Fixed</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The most frequently used size policies are <guilabel>Preferred</guilabel>"
", <guilabel>Minimum</guilabel> and <guilabel>Maximum</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:1197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vertical and horizontal stretch"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Vertical Stretch</guilabel> and <guilabel>"
"Horizontal Stretch</guilabel> properties accept integer values greater than or "
"equal to 0. These properties allow to fine-tune the behavior of size policies. "
"The default value for the properties is 0. A higher value of the stretch means "
"that the widget will be expanded more than widgets for which a lower stretch "
"value is set."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:1224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting widgets size and position by hand"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In case when your form has no main layout set for auto-positioning and "
"auto-resizing its widgets, you will probably want to modify the position and "
"size of widgets so the form can look cleaner and be easier to use. The &kexi; "
"form designer simplifies this task by offering the following groups of "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Adjusting sizes of selected widgets. The commands are available in the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guisubmenu>Adjust Widgets "
"Size</guisubmenu></menuchoice> submenu of the menubar and in the <menuchoice>"
"<guisubmenu>Adjust Widgets Size</guisubmenu></menuchoice> "
"submenu of the context menu. The toolbar's drop down button <guibutton>"
"Adjust Widgets Size</guibutton> is also available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1242
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Fit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1244
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The size of the selected widgets will be altered so each widget will be resized "
"to its preferred size and its contents; for example, a text label's size will "
"be changed to fit its text. The position of the widgets will not be changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1253 designingforms.docbook:1353
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Grid"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The size of the selected widgets will be altered so each widget's corner will "
"be placed on the form's (or other container's) grid point. The widget's "
"position can be slightly altered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1263
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Shortest"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The height of the selected widgets will be altered so that each of them will "
"have the same height as the shortest one. The position of the widgets will not "
"be changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1273
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Tallest"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The height of the selected widgets will be altered so that each of them will "
"have the same height as the tallest one. The position of the widgets will not "
"be changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1283
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Narrowest"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The width of the selected widgets will be altered so that each of them will "
"have the same height as the narrowest one. The position of the widgets will not "
"be changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1293
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Widest"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1295
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The width of the selected widgets will be altered so that each of them will "
"have the same height as the widest one. The position of the widgets will not be "
"changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Aligning positions of the selected widgets. The commands are available in the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Format</guimenu><guisubmenu>Align Widgets "
"Position</guisubmenu></menuchoice> submenu of the menubar and in the "
"<menuchoice><guisubmenu>Align Widgets Position</guisubmenu></menuchoice> "
"submenu of the context menu. The toolbar's drop down button <guibutton>"
"Align Widgets Position</guibutton> is also available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1317
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Left"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the selected widgets' left positions will be moved to the position of the "
"leftmost widget's left edge."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1326
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Right"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the selected widgets' right positions will be moved to the position of the "
"rightmost widget's right edge."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1335
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Top"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the selected widgets' top positions will be moved to the position of the "
"uppermost widget's upper edge."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: designingforms.docbook:1344
#, no-c-format
msgid "To Bottom"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the selected widgets' bottom positions will be moved to the position of the "
"bottommost widget's bottom edge."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the selected widgets' top-left corners will be moved so that they are "
"positioned in the nearest grid point."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1362
#, no-c-format
msgid "None of the above commands resizes the widgets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are also additional commands available: <guimenuitem>"
"Bring Widget to Front</guimenuitem> (i.e. above all other widgets) and "
"<guimenuitem>Send Widget to Back</guimenuitem> (i.e. below all other widgets). "
"These two commands are rarely used, as it is not common to place one widget on "
"top of an other (except when a container widget contains other widget inside). "
"Also note that clicking a widget with a mouse button is enough to bring the "
"widget to front."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: designingforms.docbook:1378
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting the tab order"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A widget's focus determines that widget's activity available using keyboard. "
"Focus is related to widgets displayed in the form's data view. Exactly one form "
"widget can have focus at the same time. The most frequent use of focus is text "
"entry (when a given text field is active, i.e. it is focused). An other example "
"is a button widget - when focused, it is possible to <quote>press</quote> "
"it using the <keycombo action=\"press\"><keycap>Enter</keycap></keycombo> "
"or <keycombo action=\"press\"><keycap>Space</keycap></keycombo> "
"key instead of a mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a few methods of making the widgets active (moving the focus to the "
"widget): clicking with a mouse button, rotating the mouse wheel over the "
"widget, or using the <keycombo action=\"press\"><keycap>Tab</keycap></keycombo> "
"key. The latter method is often used because of its speed and convenience for "
"users. Availability of the focusing methods is controlled by <guilabel>"
"Focus Policy</guilabel> property of a given widget."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a relationship between focusing (activating) widgets using <keycombo "
"action=\"press\"><keycap>Tab</keycap></keycombo> key and tab order setting of a "
"form. After pressing the <keycombo action=\"press\"><keycap>Tab</keycap>"
"</keycombo> key, the next widget should be focused, so the form should know "
"about the tab order."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1401
#, no-c-format
msgid "To alter tab order for a form's widget:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Switch to design view of the form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Execute <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Edit Tab Order...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu command. The <guilabel>"
"Edit Tab Order</guilabel> dialog will appear with settings for this form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1422
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The window contains a list with two columns: the first column displays widget "
"names, the second - types of the widgets. To make it easier to recognize "
"meaning of the names and types for the user, icons related to the types are "
"also displayed. The list contains only widgets having focus policy allowing to "
"use the <keycap>Tab</keycap> key. The window allows you to change the tab order "
"or set the automatic tab order."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1432
#, no-c-format
msgid "To change tab order, either:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click a selected widget name in the widgets list and drag it to a desired "
"position (up or down) using the mouse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click a selected widget name on the widgets list and use <guibutton>"
"Move Up</guibutton> or <guibutton>Move Down</guibutton> "
"buttons, to move the widgets to a desired position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guilabel>Handle tab order automatically</guilabel> "
"check box to set the automatic tab order for the form. If this option has been "
"switched on, any changes made to the list of widgets by hand are not taken into "
"account - &kexi; will be handling the tab orders on its own. The automatic "
"ordering means that the top-left widget will be focused first (or the top-right "
"if your operating system uses right-to-left layout), and the order comes from "
"the left to right (from the right to left, respectively) and from the top to "
"bottom."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: designingforms.docbook:1473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button to accept the changes or <guibutton>"
"Cancel</guibutton> button to dismiss the changes."
msgstr ""

